# International > Currency Format (dialog 18): symbol after the number, "-$1" negative, symbol "dm",
# 3 digits (both lists are rebuilt as each edit loses the focus), OK, then OK in International (tab
# from Change... to OK) - WIN.INI [intl] is written. Same keys as arch311-ref/scn/intl-currency.scn
# after opening. Run as intl.w16 (ARCH311_PRISTINE_INI=1, ARCH311_CLOCK="2026-10-08 09:30:24",
# applet International).
# regress: ARCH311_PRISTINE_INI=1 ARCH311_CLOCK="2026-10-08 09:30:24" sh tools/run-cp-test.sh "$TEST" "$OUT" International
# compare: intl-currency/02.png 01-open.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: intl-currency/03.png 02-currency.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: intl-currency/04.png 03-changed.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: intl-currency/05.png 04-samples.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# ini: WIN.INI intl iCurrency=1
# ini: WIN.INI intl iNegCurr=1
# ini: WIN.INI intl sCurrency=dm
# ini: WIN.INI intl iCurrDigits=3
sleep 900
shot shots/01-open.png
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key tab
key enter
sleep 600
shot shots/02-currency.png
key down
key tab
key down
key tab
type dm
key tab
type 3
key tab
sleep 300
shot shots/03-changed.png
key enter
sleep 500
shot shots/04-samples.png
key tab
key tab
key tab
key enter
sleep 400
quit
